Tiny GPT architecture

Goal
- generate text the way one specific person writes (their texting voice)
- from scratch: own tokenizer, own transformer, own training loop

Core problem and the design that answers it
- personal chat data is tiny (often < 100k words) and a model can't learn a
  language from that alone; the old version trained only on chats and produced noise
- so knowledge and style are learned separately:
  1. pretrain = general English chat from public dialogues (DailyDialog + SODA)
  2. fine-tune = the person's style, from their conversations, loss only on their turns
- this is the same recipe big chat models use (pretrain, then SFT), shrunk down

Data layer
- everything is normalized to one format: `Conversation(turns=[Turn(role, text)])`
  with role in {"me", "them"}, stored as JSONL
  - `src/tinygpt/conversation.py`: dataclasses, JSONL IO, `sessionize()`
- `sessionize()` turns a chat thread into conversations:
  - split when the silence exceeds 3 hours
  - merge consecutive messages from the same person into one turn (joined with "\n"),
    because people text a thought as several bubbles
  - drop conversations where "me" never speaks
- sources
  - `instagram_parser.py`: Instagram JSON (also fixes Instagram's latin-1 mojibake, e.g. emoji)
  - `sources.py`: WhatsApp txt (Android + iOS formats), Telegram JSON, DiscordChatExporter JSON,
    plain text (paragraphs become `me` monologues), interview JSONL
  - `public_data.py`: downloads Parquet from the Hugging Face mirror, detokenizes DailyDialog,
    randomly assigns which speaker is "me" so the model learns both sides
  - `scripts/interview.py`: cold-start data, where the user answers ~100 texts a friend might send

Tokenizer
- `src/tinygpt/bpe.py`: byte-level BPE (GPT-2/4 style), 8192 vocab
  - byte-level means no <unk>: emoji, Devanagari, Hinglish, and typos all encode
  - GPT-4 regex pre-split, so merges never cross word boundaries
  - trained with incremental pair counts + a lazy max-heap (seconds, pure Python)
  - personal text upweighted 5x during training so the user's slang gets dedicated tokens
- special tokens: <|bos|> <|them|> <|me|> <|end|>
- the old word/char tokenizers remain in `tokenizer.py` for reference

Chat format and loss mask (`chat_format.py`)
    <|bos|><|them|>hey wyd<|end|><|me|>nothing much u?<|end|>...
- pretrain: loss on every token
- fine-tune: loss only on the text + <|end|> of `me` turns; `them` turns are context only
- inference: history + "<|me|>" then sample until <|end|>

Dataset (`dataset.py`)
- `ChatStream`: all conversations concatenated into one token stream plus a bool mask
- batches are sampled by picking a trainable position first, then placing a window around it,
  so sparse "me" tokens still give every batch signal
- train/val split by whole conversation (val = unseen chats, not unseen windows)
- tokenized streams cached in `data/cache/` keyed by data mtime + tokenizer

Model (`model.py`), Llama-style small decoder
- token embedding (tied with the output head)
- N x pre-norm block: RMSNorm -> causal MHA with RoPE (SDPA / flash kernels) -> residual
                      RMSNorm -> SwiGLU MLP -> residual
- final RMSNorm -> logits
- default: 6 layers, 384 dim, 6 heads, 256 context, about 16M params (fits a 4 GB GPU with batch 32)
- generation: temperature, top-k, top-p, sign-correct repetition penalty, stop tokens,
  banned tokens (role tokens can't appear inside a reply)

Training (`trainer.py`, `scripts/train.py`)
- AdamW (betas 0.9/0.95, no decay on norm weights), warmup + cosine decay, grad clipping
- mixed precision: bf16 where supported, otherwise fp16 + GradScaler (Turing GPUs like the T2000)
- stage defaults
  - pretrain: lr 6e-4, 10k steps (~2 h on a T2000, ~2 epochs of the public data), dropout 0
  - finetune: lr 1e-4, dropout 0.1, eval every 50 steps, early stop after 6 evals without val improvement
- checkpoints: best.pt / latest.pt contain weights, configs, tokenizer, step, val loss

CLI flow
1. scripts/download_public_data.py -> data/public/dialogues.jsonl
2. scripts/interview.py and/or scripts/prepare_data.py -> data/personal/conversations.jsonl
3. scripts/train_tokenizer.py -> artifacts/tokenizer.json
4. scripts/train.py --stage pretrain -> artifacts/base/best.pt
5. scripts/train.py --stage finetune --init-from artifacts/base/best.pt -> artifacts/me/best.pt
6. scripts/chat.py / scripts/generate.py

Known limits
- 16M params: the model writes like you, but its facts and reasoning are shallow
- public data is English; Hinglish/Hindi style comes only from the fine-tune data
- style strength scales with how much of your own text you provide (20k+ words recommended)
- a fine-tuned checkpoint can memorize and repeat private messages
